<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <%- include('partials/seo-head') %>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <%- themeCSS %>
</head>
<body>
  <%- include('partials/nav') %>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <div class="hero-badge">Autovyne Legal</div>
      <h1><%= page === 'privacy' ? 'Privacy Policy' : page === 'terms' ? 'Terms of Service' : page === 'sms-compliance' ? 'SMS Compliance Review' : 'SMS Terms' %></h1>
      <p>Effective June 5, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <% if (page === 'privacy') { %>
      <section><h2>Overview</h2><p>This Privacy Policy explains how Autovyne ("Autovyne," "we," "us," or "[Company Entity Name]") handles information when businesses and their customers interact with our AI automation, audit, messaging, and support services.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Information We Collect</h2><p>We may collect names, business names, email addresses, phone numbers, websites, audit and signup form data, call and message data, AI conversation logs, and usage data. We may also collect device, browser, referral, IP address, and interaction information for security, analytics, and compliance.</p></section>
      <section><h2>How We Use Information</h2><p>We use information to provide audits, onboard customers, operate AI automation, support missed-call follow-up, send opted-in SMS notifications, provide support, improve services, analyze usage, prevent abuse, and meet legal or carrier compliance requirements.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Calls, Messages, and AI</h2><p>Calls and messages handled through Autovyne may be recorded, transcribed, analyzed, and processed by artificial intelligence. Customers are responsible for providing legally required notices and obtaining consent from their callers, leads, and customers.</p></section>
      <section><h2>SMS Consent and Sharing</h2><p>We send SMS messages only when the recipient has provided applicable consent or another lawful basis exists. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out and HELP for help.</p><p><strong>No mobile information will be shared with third parties/affiliates for marketing/promotional purposes. All other categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this information will not be shared with any third parties.</strong></p></section>
      <section><h2>Service Providers and Retention</h2><p>We may use service providers to host data, process payments, operate communications, support AI features, provide analytics, send workflow events, maintain CRM records, and support the service. We retain information for as long as reasonably necessary for service delivery, compliance, dispute resolution, security, suppression-list management, tax/accounting, and legitimate business purposes.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Privacy Rights and Requests</h2><p>Depending on location and applicable law, you may have rights to request access, correction, deletion review, portability review, opt-out or do-not-contact review, or other data-handling help. We may need to verify identity, account authority, legal requirements, and operational impact before acting on a request. SMS recipients may reply STOP at any time. Customers may use the client portal Action Center or contact us to make a privacy or account-control request.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Security and Limitations</h2><p>We use reasonable administrative, technical, and organizational safeguards for the service. No internet, telecom, AI, CRM, or payment system can be guaranteed completely secure, uninterrupted, or error-free. Customers should avoid submitting unnecessary sensitive information unless it is required for the service and authorized for processing.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Contact</h2><p>Email: <a href="mailto:kwaun.autovyne@gmail.com">kwaun.autovyne@gmail.com</a><br>Business address placeholder: [Business Address]</p></section>
    <% } else if (page === 'terms') { %>
      <section><h2>Service Description</h2><p>Autovyne provides business audits, AI automation, missed-call workflows, lead follow-up, messaging, appointment support, integrations, and related consulting services.</p></section>
      <section><h2>User Responsibilities</h2><p>You must provide accurate information, secure your accounts, use the service lawfully, and avoid abusive, deceptive, or prohibited communications. You are responsible for your business decisions and for reviewing automated output before relying on it.</p></section>
      <section><h2>AI Automation Disclaimer</h2><p>AI-generated responses, summaries, classifications, and actions may be incomplete or inaccurate. Autovyne does not guarantee that AI output will be error-free, suitable for every use, or a substitute for professional judgment.</p></section>
      <section><h2>AI Voice, Call Recording, and Transcription</h2><p>If an account uses AI voice, call recording, transcription, call summaries, or automated routing, the customer is responsible for giving legally required notices and obtaining any legally required consent from callers, staff, leads, and customers. Federal law and state law may impose different call-recording and artificial/prerecorded voice requirements. Autovyne may require scripts, disclosures, consent evidence, or workflow changes before enabling these features.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Your Customer and Lead Consent</h2><p>You are responsible for obtaining and documenting all notices, permissions, and consents required before recording calls, sending messages, placing automated calls, sending commercial email, syncing CRM data, or processing information belonging to your leads and customers. You must honor opt-out, unsubscribe, do-not-call, and do-not-contact requests promptly.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Outreach, Suppression, and Do-Not-Contact</h2><p>Autovyne may provide outreach drafts, call briefs, lead scoring, or pipeline tools, but you remain responsible for deciding who may be contacted and whether applicable telemarketing, email, SMS, state no-call, federal do-not-call, consent, and suppression-list requirements are satisfied. If a person asks not to be contacted, disputes consent, uses an opt-out keyword, or indicates the wrong number, follow-up must stop until reviewed.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Client Portal Controls</h2><p>The client portal may allow customers to submit requests such as blocking a caller, pausing follow-up, reviewing a conversation, updating automation rules, or making a privacy/data request. These controls create account records for review and do not guarantee instant changes, legal compliance, or approval of any requested action. Autovyne may need to verify consent, identity, billing status, business rules, or legal requirements before acting.</p></section>
      <section><h2>SMS Program Disclosures</h2><p>Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out and HELP for help. Consent is not a condition of purchase. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Subscriptions, Payments, Minimum Service, and Refunds</h2><p>Paid service begins after Stripe checkout is completed for automatic monthly card payments or after Autovyne approves manual monthly billing. Unless a separate written agreement says otherwise, subscriptions include an initial one-month minimum service period so Autovyne can complete onboarding, AI setup, workflow configuration, and launch support. After the first month, service may be canceled before the next billing period according to the cancellation instructions provided in the applicable order form, customer agreement, or billing portal. [Subscription plans, billing timing, cancellation process, refund policy, company entity name, and business address will be stated in the applicable order form or customer agreement.]</p></section>
      <section><h2>ROI, Metrics, and No Guarantee</h2><p>ROI calculators, recovered-revenue metrics, missed-call estimates, lead scores, and automation reports are planning and reporting tools only. They may use user-provided numbers, assumptions, observed activity, or customer-provided deal values. They are not promises, guarantees, financial advice, or proof that a specific result will occur.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Limitation of Liability</h2><p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, Autovyne and [Company Entity Name] will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or lost-profit damages arising from use of the service. Any direct liability will be limited as stated in the applicable customer agreement or as required by law.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Contact</h2><p>Email: <a href="mailto:kwaun.autovyne@gmail.com">kwaun.autovyne@gmail.com</a><br>Business address placeholder: [Business Address]</p></section>
    <% } else if (page === 'sms-compliance') { %>
      <section><h2>Purpose</h2><p>This page summarizes the Autovyne SMS program for carrier and Twilio toll-free verification review. Autovyne sends business account, audit, onboarding, missed-call automation, and service update messages only to recipients who provide applicable consent.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Business and Brand</h2><p><strong>Brand:</strong> Autovyne<br><strong>Website:</strong> <a href="/signup">https://autovyne.com/signup</a><br><strong>Contact:</strong> <a href="mailto:kwaun.autovyne@gmail.com">kwaun.autovyne@gmail.com</a><br><strong>Business address:</strong> [Business Address]</p></section>
      <section><h2>SMS Program Name</h2><p>Autovyne SMS Alerts &amp; Automation.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Message Types</h2><p>Messages may include account alerts, audit updates, onboarding updates, missed-call alerts, lead follow-up notices, appointment reminders, customer communication workflow updates, support follow-up, and service status notifications.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Opt-In Workflow</h2><p>Businesses opt in by visiting the public Autovyne signup page at <a href="/signup">/signup</a> and checking an unchecked SMS consent checkbox near the phone number field. The checkbox is not pre-selected. The signup page displays the following consent language before submission:</p><p><strong>By checking this box, I consent to receive SMS messages from Autovyne related to my account, audit request, onboarding, missed-call automation, and service updates. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out and HELP for help. Consent is not a condition of purchase. View our Privacy Policy and SMS Terms.</strong></p></section>
      <section><h2>Consent Recordkeeping</h2><p>Autovyne stores SMS consent status, consent timestamp, phone number, form source, IP address when available, user agent when available, and the exact consent text shown at submission. If the checkbox is not checked, the request may still be submitted, but the contact is not marked as SMS opted in.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Sample Messages</h2><p><strong>Audit update:</strong> Autovyne: Your missed-call audit request was received. We will review your account setup next. Reply STOP to opt out or HELP for help.</p><p><strong>Onboarding update:</strong> Autovyne: Your onboarding checklist has been updated in your client portal. Message frequency varies. Reply STOP to opt out or HELP for help.</p><p><strong>Missed-call alert:</strong> Autovyne: Missed-call automation detected a new lead follow-up item for your business. Log in to your portal to review. Reply STOP to opt out or HELP for help.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Opt-Out and Help</h2><p>Recipients can reply STOP to opt out and HELP for help. Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Consent is not a condition of purchase. Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Privacy and Data Sharing</h2><p><strong>No mobile information will be shared with third parties/affiliates for marketing/promotional purposes. All other categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this information will not be shared with any third parties.</strong></p><p>See the <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, and <a href="/sms-terms">SMS Terms</a>.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Compliance References</h2><p>Autovyne designs its SMS and outreach controls around consent, opt-out, and suppression-list principles reflected in federal TCPA/FCC rules, FTC telemarketing guidance, CAN-SPAM guidance, recurring-billing guidance, AI-claims guidance, and applicable state no-call laws. These references do not replace legal review for any specific customer workflow.</p></section>
    <% } else { %>
      <section><h2>Program</h2><p><strong>Program name:</strong> Autovyne SMS Alerts &amp; Automation.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Message Types</h2><p>Messages may include account alerts, audit updates, onboarding updates, missed-call alerts, lead follow-up, appointment reminders, and customer communication workflows.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Frequency and Charges</h2><p>Message frequency varies. Message and data rates may apply. Consent is not a condition of purchase.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Opt Out and Help</h2><p>Reply STOP to opt out. Reply HELP for help. You may also contact <a href="mailto:kwaun.autovyne@gmail.com">kwaun.autovyne@gmail.com</a>. Autovyne may send one confirmation message after an opt-out request where allowed, then messaging should stop unless a lawful basis and updated consent record exists.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Carrier Disclaimer</h2><p>Carriers are not liable for delayed or undelivered messages.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Consent Records</h2><p>Autovyne keeps consent records for program verification, customer support, compliance, suppression-list management, dispute resolution, and operational security. Consent records may include phone number, timestamp, form source, IP address when available, user agent when available, and the exact consent language shown.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Related Policies</h2><p>Review our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>, <a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a>, and <a href="/sms-compliance">SMS Compliance Review</a>.</p></section>
    <% } %>
  </main>
  <%- include('partials/footer') %>
  <%- analyticsSnippet %>
</body>
</html>
